Changes to OCCT (V8_0_1) for the Open CAD Viewer. Applied by wasm/scripts/build-occt.sh.

- STEP: convert CSG and swept solids, which OCCT read but never turned into shapes, so parts
  made of them loaded empty (AP203 e2 conformance options co20 and co72; AP214 allows them too):
  csg_solid and boolean_result trees of block, right_angular_wedge, right_circular_cylinder,
  right_circular_cone, sphere, torus and planar half-spaces; extruded and revolved areas and
  faces; solid replicas. Done in STEPControl_ActorRead with BRepPrimAPI and BRepAlgoAPI, so
  TKDESTEP now links TKPrim and TKBO. A half-space without a box is made as a box covering the
  other operands of its boolean on the material side.
  Polyline outlines are split at their corners before sweeping (OCCT reads a polyline as one
  degree-1 B-spline), so each segment sweeps to its own face instead of one creased face that
  meshed to tens of thousands of triangles.
- STEP: boolean_result operands were read as solid models only, and csg_solid roots as boolean
  results only. Any other operand (a primitive, a half-space, a nested boolean) was dropped, so
  CSG trees came out empty even before conversion. Now read as whichever type they are.

